<p>U.S. forces said they destroyed six Iranian small boats and intercepted Iranian cruise missiles and drones on Monday during President Trump’s “Project Freedom” operation to move commercial shipping through the Strait of Hormuz. Iran denied the U.S. account, while Iranian state-linked reports said a U.S. Navy vessel was hit near the strait; U.S. Central Command denied that any U.S. Navy ship was struck. The exchange followed an early-April U.S.-Iran cease-fire after the Feb. 28 start of U.S.-Israeli attacks on Iran and Tehran’s restrictions on the waterway, according to Reuters reporting carried by Al-Monitor and AP reporting carried by ABC and NPR. The United Arab Emirates also said it came under Iranian missile and drone attack. President Trump told a Fox News reporter that Iran would be “blown off the face of the earth” if it attacked U.S. Navy ships in the region, while Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi criticized Washington’s approach and warned against trying to settle the crisis militarily.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/P1lV-_nP1E25pUwVgjGRMZwaPAey3PRCAaRz4T1mpqFcqw2N_quL0KZEJx87_17U3wqeUf5-E2Mu-7PH4S946KoKW-8dDNI8NbKD81i3mAlo6BVCKSqyof-pG9thIDcQ1cOlvXXz02jM-W5m2WYneBqGzJCmS3EIaX9gfojUUiK6Eb5hze_EKwXO_f5Bd8ty4R4QyQxIb0zKOSOSWpY' alt='Ships and tankers in the Strait of Hormuz in April.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Force size: The U.S. operation involved 15,000 troops, destroyers, more than 100 land- and sea-based aircraft and undersea assets, the U.S. military said.</li><li>Destroyer transit: U.S. defense officials identified the USS Truxtun and USS Mason as the two destroyers that led the transit into the Persian Gulf.</li></ul><blockquote>Makes clear that there’s no military solution to a political crisis - Abbas Araghchi</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Central Command: Adm. Brad Cooper said he “strongly advised” Iranian forces to stay clear of U.S. military assets as the operation proceeds. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.